{"id": 96, "ts": 1781252625.2928176, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I appreciate the strong case made for Candidate\u202fC, especially his reliability and calmness under pressure. However, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the safer overall choice for a long\u2011distance pilot. B\u2019s very conscientious nature and excellent stress handling directly address the operational reliability and stress\u2011resilience criteria that are non\u2011negotiable for international routes. His ability to assess weather conditions and his excellent computer skills also demonstrate solid technical competence, which is essential for complex, long\u2011haul flight planning.\nWhile B does have a relatively weak memory for numbers and has been noted to make nasty remarks about colleagues, these issues are more manageable through procedural safeguards and targeted interpersonal coaching than the deeper concerns we see with C. C\u2019s egocentric reputation, difficulty communicating ideas, and lack of willingness to pursue further education suggest a limited capacity for crew cooperation, professional communication, and adaptability\u2014areas that are critical for sustained safety and team performance in the cockpit.\nGiven that B\u2019s interpersonal shortcomings appear less entrenched and can be mitigated, whereas C\u2019s adaptability deficits may persist and affect crew dynamics, I continue to recommend **Candidate\u202fB** for the position."}
